+| 6167d30af | 2026-11-23 | Mach4 keeps G84 tap feed precision and refuses written pitch errors above 0.01 percent (#3701, PR #3731) | 0.26.0 |
+| 9dfcc7ac2 | 2026-11-23 | New library machine "Ooznest WorkBee 1000x1500 (Estlcam)": X 1200, Y 770, Z 88 mm, the smaller of the owner's and Ooznest's published travel; the owner must confirm the travel, and no post is named until the Estlcam post (#3735) ships (#3038, PR #3736) | 0.26.0 |
+| 4d0e09fd4 | 2026-11-23 | Engrave operations now support Do not touch protection surfaces (UI, MCP, project roundtrip, and motion avoidance) (#3349, PR #3549) | 0.26.0 |
+| 01e177bf5 | 2026-11-23 | Typed text in a TrueType outline font becomes a profile of closed shapes (letter holes included) for a pocket, V-carve or cut-out: MCP tool `insert_outline_text`, one undo step; unreadable or CFF fonts, missing glyphs, overlapping outlines and nested outlines that the font's nonzero fill does not make holes, and fonts that exceed the part, point or coordinate limits are refused by name (#3072, PR #3395) | 0.26.0 |
+| 47aa341ff | 2026-11-23 | 2D Offset and 2D Pocket Outside: a later pass that starts at a dead end now enters by a ramp along the pass at the entry's ramp angle (3 degrees by default), not by a plunge or helix into uncut stock. At a dead end, the worst sampled start cuts with about 25 percent of the tool disc in uncut stock (12.6 mm2 of 50.3 mm2 for the 4.780 mm band), so the zig-zag cuts a slot at nearly full tool width at 3 degrees. A dead end too short for the ramp cuts the area in the Auto order, and the path names it (#3567, PR #3577) | 0.26.0 |
+| 65b52cca6 | 2026-11-23 | Post: generic ISO abrasive-waterjet post (`waterjet-iso.cps`), WATERJET / JET stream records with `onJetOn` / `onJetOff`, CR LF output (`lineEnding`), `machine.travel`, `programBounds` and arc linearization (`linearizeArcs`) for scripts (#1882, PR #3046) | 0.26.0 |
+| 2dd93d7ad | 2026-11-23 | Saved cut recipes: save an operation's settings under a name and apply them to new geometry in one undoable step (MCP `save_cut_recipe`, `list_cut_recipes`, `apply_cut_recipe`); a recipe whose tool or material is gone is refused by name (#3073, PR #3399) | 0.26.0 |
+| a59faa5b5 | 2026-11-23 | Multi-Axis Deburr operation: breaks steep and vertical edges with a tilted chamfer mill (5-axis tilt or 4-axis rotary plane), tilts the holder clear inside a max tilt, refuses unreachable edges by name, and refuses stock that is not the source model or a setup with other parts (#1894, PR #3283) | 0.26.0 |
+| dac6a896b | 2026-11-23 | Added Siemens Sinumerik 810M 3-axis milling post, EMCO VMC-200 machine profile, and owner air-cut kit (#2888, PR #3317) | 0.26.0 |
+| f81bcac8c | 2026-11-23 | New "G-EDM Wire EDM" post: 2-axis wire contours for G-EDM controllers (G-RBLv3) in Grbl-family words, with no `edm.codes` (spark power is set at the controller); taper, 4-axis, skims and G41 / G42 are refused by name; not verified on a control (#2700, PR #3312) | 0.26.0 |
+| 33685374f | 2026-11-23 | New built-in post "RichAuto DSP A11" for RichAuto A11 routers (Laguna Swift, Grizzly): .mmg files with N numbers, one tool, drilling as plain moves, named refusals for tapping, cutter compensation and probing (#1914, PR #3294) | 0.26.0 |
+| 2de071415 | 2026-11-23 | 2D Adaptive (Spiral and Trochoidal) honours "Do not touch": the full tool (flutes, shank, holder) stays clear of each protected face or edge by the clearance, or the operation is refused with the item named (#3346, PR #3656) | 0.26.0 |
+| ddc4d8274 | 2026-11-23 | The Haas post writes each feed with its decimals (three in mm/min, four in in/min), so a G84 tap feed gives the exact thread pitch; a tap whose written F and S cannot give the pitch within 0.01 percent is refused by name (#3692, #3694, PR #3700) | 0.26.0 |
+| 81643a2a4 | 2026-11-23 | CL toolpath transforms: translate, XY turn, A/B axis turn and vertical-plane mirror (G2/G3 and G41/G42 swap, or a climb-preserving pass reversal), with named refusals (#3011, PR #3308) | 0.26.0 |
+| 3fc0e017b | 2026-11-23 | The Haas post writes each feed word with a decimal point (`F600.`), so the feed is correct at each value of Haas Setting 77 (#3681, PR #3689) | 0.26.0 |
+| 4c0a8dfe3 | 2026-11-23 | A linked model with a relative path is now read from the folder of the project file, not from the folder the program started in (#3686, PR #3687) | 0.26.0 |
+| 9a4cf16f9 | 2026-11-23 | The 2D Adaptive operation has rest machining from the previous operations: it cuts only what the earlier operations of the setup left, and each plunge stands where their stock proves the cutter clear (set through MCP or the project file; the page rows follow in #2884) (#1446, #2885, PR #2890) | 0.26.0 |
+| b215df411 | 2026-11-23 | 2D Contour with tabs: the levels above the tabs now start where the first tab window enters, so that window dives into the cut of the level above and not into uncut sheet (#3453, #3678, #3679, PR #3684) | 0.26.0 |
+| 82db54282 | 2026-11-23 | macOS release packages can use Developer ID signing and Apple notarization when the release credentials are configured (#1642, PR #3398) | 0.26.0 |
+| 10a0a39c0 | 2026-11-23 | Cutting tools skip reserved probe pockets and cannot use reserved tool names. Breaking: project files step to version 78; older builds refuse them (#2604, PR #3284) | 0.26.0 |
+| d1176cda7 | 2026-11-23 | DXF import reads AutoCAD 2000 (AC1015) files with CLASSES, THUMBNAILIMAGE, ACDSDATA sections and layout objects, and refuses an entity record in a section that holds no geometry (#3450, PR #3672) | 0.26.0 |
